msgid "Bitmap of what Logger backend types to enable\\. Block\\-based logging is available on SITL and boards with dataflash chips\\. Multiple backends can be selected\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43769
#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:76400
#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:76798
#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:77196
#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:77594
#: 23b24d88eb964a5081374a83625b2982
#: 04af554719fa41e98608f5bd2c91a857
#: 6d2123bf9af744338c0d0d52ed1e59f4
#: ccf6d54791f54029af845db0a23f8c40
#: 62fd017b650a4571b22b2021a1b36c25
msgid "File"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43773
#: 79f6be9dc68e401aa37f48e0ced2968d
msgid "Block"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43784
#: d292d96905104e21922e08bdee500f43
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_BUFSIZE: Logging File and Block Backend buffer size max \\(in kibibytes\\)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43787
#: 0e79070bfc804cada872029b4ca4ea38
msgid "The File and Block backends use a buffer to store data before writing to the block device\\.  Raising this value may reduce \\\"gaps\\\" in your SD card logging but increases memory usage\\.  This buffer size may be reduced to free up available memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43793
#: 6ad6e1fe9d30433cae913b86fd998ff9
msgid "4 to 200"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43793
#: 1c4ad9e04d884c7bb12a2a5f13f6f15f
msgid "kibibytes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43802
#: 0b4c0c91722f4ffabea70ce1270bb492
msgid "LOG\\_DISARMED: Enable logging while disarmed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43805
#: 822c9683e96c43c3b95d31d9d9c50013
msgid "If LOG\\_DISARMED is set to 1 then logging will be enabled at all times including when disarmed\\. Logging before arming can make for very large logfiles but can help a lot when tracking down startup issues and is necessary if logging of EKF replay data is selected via the LOG\\_REPLAY parameter\\. If LOG\\_DISARMED is set to 2\\, then logging will be enabled when disarmed\\, but not if a USB connection is detected\\. This can be used to prevent unwanted data logs being generated when the vehicle is connected via USB for log downloading or parameter changes\\. If LOG\\_DISARMED is set to 3 then logging will happen while disarmed\\, but if the vehicle never arms then the logs using the filesystem backend will be discarded on the next boot\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43818
#: 656b75e3cf884c3f94fb9a1157f8ff59
msgid "Disabled on USB connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43820
#: 83bd9de73cb54ebfaa65ff95f247c38b
msgid "Discard log on reboot if never armed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43831
#: 2e1afc09a2b94cca90eb2cdfb2a6208a
msgid "LOG\\_REPLAY: Enable logging of information needed for Replay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43834
#: 64839295c9914e3ea8d3c4002b8b2252
msgid "If LOG\\_REPLAY is set to 1 then the EKF2 and EKF3 state estimators will log detailed information needed for diagnosing problems with the Kalman filter\\. LOG\\_DISARMED must be set to 1 or 2 or else the log will not contain the pre\\-flight data required for replay testing of the EKF\\'s\\. It is suggested that you also raise LOG\\_FILE\\_BUFSIZE to give more buffer space for logging and use a high quality microSD card to ensure no sensor data is lost\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43856
#: 57f66bfc9d1045fdab6c5ae6b0cee395
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_DSRMROT: Stop logging to current file on disarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43859
#: 28dcefa907b342a08647f5fc4dc5a4b6
msgid "When set\\, the current log file is closed when the vehicle is disarmed\\.  If LOG\\_DISARMED is set then a fresh log will be opened\\. Applies to the File and Block logging backends\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43881
#: 9ef7e0b5b3354a1eaf6436187640c36f
msgid "LOG\\_MAV\\_BUFSIZE: Maximum AP\\_Logger MAVLink Backend buffer size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43885
#: 278a216152534251a8d4ad3630be7539
msgid "Maximum amount of memory to allocate to AP\\_Logger\\-over\\-mavlink"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43891
#: 1f52435a1b3f45848f6b5bf74992ab91
msgid "kilobytes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43900
#: 77883d2d523441608a7d0d55864e49aa
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_TIMEOUT: Timeout before giving up on file writes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43903
#: 0d92e4f38b374a7a9d692d140a658c1f
msgid "This controls the amount of time before failing writes to a log file cause the file to be closed and logging stopped\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43918
#: bd5da60c8c40459997527491fd6d1d72
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_MB\\_FREE: Old logs on the SD card will be deleted to maintain this amount of free space"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43921
#: dbe5f72aed2447cabab65f0d32a2e043
msgid "Set this such that the free space is larger than your largest typical flight log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43927
#: d37469d151054c0897507bcfc34666e2
msgid "2 to 1000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43927
#: aa174bb66c644dbcab55ea170a02a0d6
msgid "megabyte"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43936
#: acfe34606f334f92a772978c4cc4786e
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_RATEMAX: Maximum logging rate for file backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43939
#: 57508a319e7e4ba58097eaa115a156ac
msgid "This sets the maximum rate that streaming log messages will be logged to the file backend\\. A value of zero means that rate limiting is disabled\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43945
#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43963
#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43981
#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43999
#: 03753dc8f86449bea7a2b5f341471293
#: a998704180904bcbbfd411bdb557b232
#: 04f62ba3d6394de2ac1fe489269f8b5e
#: f5833deefa8f4f72926ed1a89e1bf329
msgid "0 to 1000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43954
#: 1fc205b088654ee4a052ab45058880f3
msgid "LOG\\_MAV\\_RATEMAX: Maximum logging rate for mavlink backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43957
#: 55a229212fda45ecac3a03fa6bedd5fb
msgid "This sets the maximum rate that streaming log messages will be logged to the mavlink backend\\. A value of zero means that rate limiting is disabled\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43972
#: 8a2409b75eb74c84b2365dad0665a585
msgid "LOG\\_BLK\\_RATEMAX: Maximum logging rate for block backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43975
#: cee178254ba84be8aa69af58d3df3d1e
msgid "This sets the maximum rate that streaming log messages will be logged to the block backend\\. A value of zero means that rate limiting is disabled\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43990
#: b516d844a06f473588f517b3649fc493
msgid "LOG\\_DARM\\_RATEMAX: Maximum logging rate when disarmed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:43993
#: f632ccda42ec416c94ebf165102d1067
msgid "This sets the maximum rate that streaming log messages will be logged to any backend when disarmed\\. A value of zero means that the normal backend rate limit is applied\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:44008
#: 273695ebe6254dbcb03b7da401c00de8
msgid "LOG\\_MAX\\_FILES: Maximum number of log files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:44013
#: 46d76b059e724102bb222bfabad72ee1
